Apache Qpid Dispatch Router 1.19.0 Remote Stack Overflow


Vendor: The Apache Software Foundation
Product web page: https://qpid.apache.org/components/dispatch-router/index.html
Affected version: 1.19.0

Summary: A high-performance, lightweight AMQP 1.0 message router, written
in C and built on Qpid Proton. It provides flexible and scalable interconnect
between any AMQP endpoints, whether they be clients, brokers or other AMQP-enabled
services.

Desc: Apache Qpid Dispatch suffers from a denial-of-service vulnerability caused
by unbounded recursion in its AMQP field parser. The parser recurses once per
nested child with no depth limit when parsing message annotations, so a remote
peer can send a deeply nested AMQP message and exhaust the stack, crashing the
router. This issue is tracked as CVE-2026-88763 assigned by Red Hat as the CNA
against the maintained downstream component skupper-router (Red Hat Service Interconnect),
which carries the same AMQP field parser. The Apache Qpid Dispatch project is
frozen (development moved to skupper-router). Red Hat notes that exploitation
requires a valid x.509 certificate signed by the interconnect certificate authority,
i.e. a peer already admitted to the mutually authenticated network, can crash the
router.

